course: dictionary
lesson: 10711
title: Untreated: not yet cared for
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Untreated has two parts. The un- at the start means not, and treated means dealt with or cared for. So untreated means not dealt with yet. Look at the words around it to be sure.
explain: «If it's left untreated, the weak eye's sight can stay poor for life.» The clue is left. Nobody has given the eye any care, so the problem stays and may last. Untreated is about something that is not being looked after.
explain: The same idea works for other things. «Untreated sewage flowed into the river» means dirty water went into the river without being cleaned first. Untreated wood has not been painted or protected, so it can rot in the rain. Always try your meaning in the sentence to check it fits.
fact: Un- at the start of a word means not, so untreated means not treated.
fact: «Untreated» can mean a sickness or injury has not been given medical care.
fact: «Untreated» can mean water, sewage or materials have not been cleaned or processed with chemicals.
fact: «Untreated» can mean wood has not been painted or protected.
fact: «Untreated» often warns that something could cause harm if it is left alone.
exercise: «If it's left untreated, the weak eye's sight can stay poor for life.» What does untreated mean here? | *Has not been given medical care | Has been kept warm and dry | Has been cured and is completely well | Has been painted to look nice
exercise: «Untreated sewage flowed into the river.» What had not been cleaned? | The rain | The riverbank | *The sewage | The river
exercise: Dad says the untreated wood will rot if it is left outside. What does untreated wood mean? | Wood that has been painted twice | Wood that is wet from the rain | Wood that is brand new from the shop | *Wood that has not been painted or protected
test: A doctor says an illness left untreated can get worse. What does untreated mean? | Fully cured | Very hot to touch | Painted and shiny | *Not given medical care
test: Untreated water has not been what? | Poured into a jug | Frozen into ice | Heated to boiling point | *Cleaned or processed with chemicals
exam: What does it mean when untreated sewage goes into a river? | It goes into the river and turns into fish | It goes into the river and makes the water clean | It stops flowing before it reaches the river | *It goes into the river without being cleaned first
